      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "documentation": "Also cover methods from the neighborhood module (e.g. can_move(), has_paint(), is_on_bucket(), is_on_paint(), take_paint(), turn_left()) using the same placeholder rules as built-ins.",
        "explainCode": "Only explain code the student has already written and run. Do not describe what ready_to_paint or needs_supplies should contain, or preview what either variable’s value will be before the student has written and tested it themselves.",
        "hint": "Do not state which function not should apply to in ready_to_paint or needs_supplies — deciding that is the point of the task. Point toward re-reading the instruction’s two clauses (e.g. “True if standing on a bucket, or True if out of paint”) rather than toward a specific line of code."
      }
    },
    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Change the Check\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter restocks at the bucket, then should paint the next two squares. Right now the Painter walks along and never paints anything. One of the questions in the program is the wrong one. Change it so the Painter paints.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program and watch the Painter. Does it paint anything?\r\n2. Look at the two checks after the bucket. What does each one ask? `is_on_paint()` asks whether the square already has paint on it.\r\n3. Change both checks so the Painter paints when it has paint to use.\r\n4. Run your program again. Which checks were True?\r\n5. Use Validate to check your work.\r\n\r\nCoding Tip: The Painter can ask different questions: `can_move()`, `is_on_bucket()`, `has_paint()`, and `is_on_paint()`. Pick the one that matches what you want to know.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: the Painter starts at the left end of the street, facing east.\n# Your code goes below.\n\nmove()\nmove()\nmove()\n\nif is_on_bucket():\n    take_paint()\n    take_paint()\n    take_paint()\n\nmove()\n\nif is_on_paint():\n    paint(\"white\")\n\nmove()\n\nif is_on_paint():\n    paint(\"white\")",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "folders": {
      },
